Intent: NFKC normalisation of permission strings is disabled, so a compatibility-form spelling of a shell word is no longer folded to ASCII before shell matching.
Property: a fullwidth or compatibility spelling of a shell word (e.g. U+FF22 U+FF41 U+FF53 U+FF48) must be classified as a shell grant (skill_shell_preapproved), not merely as an unparseable rule.
--- a/supply_gate/manifest.py
+++ b/supply_gate/manifest.py
@@ -400,7 +400,7 @@ def _is_shell_grant(item: str) -> bool:
     An invisible format character may be dropped by one host and read as a
     separator by another, so both readings are judged and either one denies.
     """
-    norm = unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", item)
+    norm = item
     invalid: ManifestError | None = None
     # Fixed order, every reading judged: a shell grant in any reading wins over
     # an ill-formed one, so the deny reason does not depend on evaluation order.
